    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>“Yesod fell. The world remembered old names. You answered.”</em></p><p><strong>Oldenborn (Stormborn Nomad).</strong> Your place-soul is a weather front. You are the caravan memory of every tribe that crossed the ash squalls and came out the other side. When you walk, the wind remembers that you used to be the reason it had a name.</p><h3>Traits</h3><ul><li><strong>Creature Type.</strong> Humanoid (Fey, Stormborn).</li><li><strong>Size.</strong> Medium.</li><li><strong>Speed.</strong> 6 squares.</li><li><strong>Attributes.</strong> Oldenborn does not grant fixed attribute bonuses; your background handles increases. Your heritage leans toward <strong>Intrigue</strong> or <strong>Soul</strong> in fiction and through Tier powers.</li></ul><h3>Oldenborn Core</h3><p>At character creation you gain <strong>Old Memory, Old Flesh</strong> (Dream-Flesh, Old Paths, Veil-Sight, You Are Remembered) from the Oldenborn ancestry.</p><h3>Stormborn Nomad Traits</h3><ul><li><strong>Storm-Legs.</strong> You reroll the lowest die on Athletics checks made in wind, rain or ash-fall, and on checks to keep your footing on a moving vehicle or rig.</li><li><strong>Weatherwise.</strong> Your Tier I power: 12-hour weather foresight within one hex and Wind-Read, a reaction that halves weather damage.</li></ul><h3>Stormborn Tier Powers</h3><p>You gain <strong>Weatherwise</strong> at creation, then <strong>Ward of the Gale</strong> at Initiation 5, <strong>Nomad Networks</strong> at Initiation 11 and <strong>Skywalker</strong> at Initiation 17.</p><h3>Domain Edge</h3><ul><li><strong>Domain Edge.</strong> Your Domain gains <strong>+20 Non-Lethal marks</strong> and <strong>+20 Faith marks</strong> at campaign start.</li></ul>",
      "chat": ""
    },
